{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And they turned and went up.</b> Toward the north, for all who travel from south to north go up, by way of the Bashan, between the land of the children of Ammon and the Jordan. <b>And they turned and went up.</b> To Og — since all his land was part of the land of Canaan, they did not offer him peace, because it was stated concerning them: לא תחיה כל נשמה. But Sihon — since part of his land was from the territory of Moab and Ammon — they did offer him peace." "<b>And he went out</b>, etc. Already explained in the pericah לך לך — for what reason he merited to live so long, from Noah until Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:10.879877109Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}